SUMMARY:Silverbacks' Annual Improvised Holiday Show
LOCATION:Cité des Arts\, 109 Vine St\, Lafayette
DESCRIPTION:It’s nearly that time of year again! On *Wednesday*\, Decembe
 r 9th\, Silverbacks Improv Theatre will interpret their signature improvis
 ations through the lens of a brand new\, completely made up Holiday!\nFor 
 this show\, each of the performers will be wearing a Holiday Sweater and i
 nvite the audience to do the same. ANY Holiday themed items are welcome 
 – the audience is invited to wear their finest Christmas\, Easter\, Mard
 i Gras\, or even Groundhog Day sweaters to add to the fun.\nOur previously
  invented and celebrated holidays are “Paper-Clip Appreciation Day” (2
 012)\, “Garden Gnome Day” (2013)\, “Leonardo DaVinci’s Mother’s 
 Birthday” (2014)\, “Picasso-Palooza” (2015)\, “St. Lampshades Day
 ” (2016)\, “Structural Support Day” (2017)\, and “Snowpocalypse: T
 he Anniversary of that One Day It Snowed in Louisiana” (2018)\, "Aggress
 ive Yoga Day" (2019)\, "Don't Fit Day" (2020)\, "Balloon Heritage Day" (20
 22)\, "Sunphobia Day" (2023)\, "Arbor Day II" (2024)\, and "Hydro-Celebrat
 ion" (2025).\nWEDNESDAY\, December 9\, 2026\n7:30 pm at Cite des Arts\, MA
 IN Stage\nTickets are $15 online or at the door!\n\nhttps://happeningnext.
 com/event/silverbacks-annual-improvised-holiday-show-eid3a0ebmlpc7
